  "body": "Lathe axis fit sets off-centre features aside (issue #71).\n\n**What changed**\n- New `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/axis_robust.rs` (trimmed least squares / RANSAC consensus refit, Pottmann & Randrup): after the plain fit, keep the facets whose normal lines pass within the fit's tolerance (`REL_TOL·rho`, 3% of the mean radius) of the candidate axis (and facets along the axis), refit the line and the #62 refinement on them, up to 4 rounds until the kept set settles. Each refit must still pass the existing full judgement (90% concurrency share, coarseness) - it can only move an axis the part already earns. A plain revolve returns the plain fit bit for bit. Guard: kept < 50% of area or < 8 facets -> plain fit, untrusted.\n- `axis::fit` unchanged in signature; new `axis::fit_report` returns robust and plain axes, set-aside share, trust flag.\n- `spindle_law.rs`: a trusted reading keeps the misplaced-part message with \"(read on the revolved surface; X% of the part's surface - keyways, flats, holes - set aside)\"; an untrusted one says off-centre features bias the fit and moving the work offset cannot fix it.\n\n**Measured** (72-segment D20 shaft, keyway Z0..Z10, floor x = 8): 5.18 mm keyway 0.153 -> 0.000 mm off, 0.9% set aside; 10 mm keyway 0.058 -> 0.000 mm, 0.35%.\n\n**Pinned by** `lathe_spindle_keyed::{a_keyed_shaft_on_g54_passes_the_spindle_law_and_generates, a_keyed_shaft_off_g54_is_refused_as_misplaced_naming_the_set_aside_share}` (both failed on main) + `axis_robust` unit tests (plain revolve bit for bit; keyway no longer drags the axis, direction kept).\n\n**Gates**: quick gate green; app lathe/turning/rotary suites, golden_cl, motion lib + rotary/multiaxis/turning suites green; clippy clean; no golden changed.\n\n**Limit**: a large keyway (> ~10% of the surface) is still refused as not revolved before the robust pass runs - #110.\n\nChangelog: fix(motion,app): the lathe axis fit sets keyways, flats and cross holes aside, so a correctly placed keyed shaft passes the spindle law; the refusal names the set-aside share and gives move-the-offset advice only for a misplaced part\n\nFixes #71\n",
